Mood Tracking Application is an Android-based application designed to help users record, monitor, and analyze their daily moods and activities. 
This application aims to increase self-awareness of emotional patterns and support mental well-being through structured mood tracking and visual insights.

📱 Features
Daily Mood Tracking:
Users can record their daily mood along with feelings and activities.

Mood History:
View past mood records organized by date in a calendar or list format.

Statistics & Visualization:
Displays mood trends using charts and summaries to help users understand emotional patterns over time.

Activity & Feeling Management:
Users can add and manage custom activities and feelings stored locally.

Data Export & Import:
Export mood data to CSV / PDF / Excel and re-import data when needed.

Offline Storage:
All data is stored locally using Room Database, ensuring privacy and offline access.

🛠️ Tech Stack
Platform: 
Android

Language: 
Kotlin

Architecture:
MVVM (Model–View–ViewModel)

Database: 
Room (SQLite)

UI Components:
RecyclerView
Fragment
Material Design
Data Visualization: Chart Library

Data Storage:
Room Database
SharedPreferences (for lightweight data)

🔄 Application Flow:
User selects mood, feeling, and activity
Data is stored in local database
Mood history and statistics are generated automatically
Users can export or import data as needed

🎯 Purpose:
This application is developed as part of an academic project to support:
Mood self-monitoring
Mental health awareness
Research on mood pattern analysis using mobile applications

🚀 Installation:
Clone this repository:
git clone https://github.com/Kyizaky/MyMood.git
Open the project in Android Studio
Sync Gradle
Run the app on an emulator or physical device
